title: 'umbrella: do not bundle test utilities into the node feature'
doc:
  - audience:
      - Node Dev
      - Runtime Dev
    description: |
      The `node` feature of the `polkadot-sdk` umbrella crate no longer enables `asset-test-utils`,
      `bridge-hub-test-utils`, `emulated-integration-tests-common` and
      `parachains-runtimes-test-utils`. These crates pulled `assets-common` and `pallet-revive`
      into every node built on the umbrella. With `runtime-benchmarks`, they also built
      `pallet-revive-fixtures`.

      The crates are still part of the umbrella. Code that uses them through the umbrella must now
      enable their features explicitly, for example `features = ["node", "asset-test-utils"]`.
crates:
  - name: polkadot-sdk
    bump: major
  - name: asset-test-utils
    bump: none
  - name: bridge-hub-test-utils
    bump: none
  - name: emulated-integration-tests-common
    bump: none
  - name: parachains-runtimes-test-utils
    bump: none
